{"chapter": "moduli", "node_kind": "section_title", "parent_tag": "0DMD", "placeholders": {}, "render": {"prefix": "\\section{", "suffix": "}\n\\label{section-picard-functor}"}, "risk_level": "R1", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:907262a6c92d36cd53d9156c3e952301dd165a6634ccc9557e8887ca7698a15d", "source_text": "Properties of the Picard functor", "source_text_hash": "sha256:000e7f36dbcb5e6ca573cbdc9f31997b3e53cdd7027b0e1c5488daa35abc505c", "unit_id": "tag:0DMD:title"}
{"chapter": "moduli", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "0DMD", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$f : X \\to B$", "MATH_0002": "$T/B$", "MATH_0003": "$$\n\\mathcal{O}_T \\longrightarrow f_{T, *}\\mathcal{O}_{X_T}\n$$", "MATH_0004": "$\\Picardfunctor_{X/B}$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{quot-proposition-pic-functor}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:439710ec635e1e430bda5a226a16881c8a6ffc5a11479c5d22326ffc9a15d3eb", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:52b933b17a123ada6caee7d65e36f85c78de25fe47201b052bc3cff2a79c9e5f", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nLet <MATH_0001> be a morphism of algebraic spaces which is flat,\nproper, and of finite presentation such that moreover for every <MATH_0002>\nthe canonical map\n<MATH_0003>\nis an isomorphism. Then the Picard functor <MATH_0004> is an\nalgebraic space, see Quot, Proposition <REF_0001>.\nThere is a closed relationship with the Picard stack.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:f06ecae7ae46a4621a62babed6e47722548472fc5c92eee150ea53d64a39246b", "unit_id": "tag:0DMD:prose-0001"}
{"chapter": "moduli", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "0DMD", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\Picardstack_{X/B} \\to \\Picardfunctor_{X/B}$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-pic-gerbe-over-pic-functor}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:b6c4a01ca6e85d2b5eafeb1a6f4cf66553eec7413ca44c083f25613a3595eb8b", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:4af6125f32f00e4d27ab1991360fafa8a14fc9598ce69d28664cf632b62166eb", "source_text": "The morphism <MATH_0001>\nturns the Picard stack into a gerbe over the Picard functor.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:df3bd8c37a8dc0f8bfe8535f219f4a1a3b96a40813c16657a95a455bd8877aa8", "unit_id": "tag:0DME:statement"}
{"chapter": "moduli", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "0DMD", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\Picardstack_{X/B} \\to \\Picardfunctor_{X/B}$", "MATH_0002": "$\\xi \\in \\Picardfunctor_{X/B}(U)$", "MATH_0003": "$U$", "MATH_0004": "$B$", "MATH_0005": "$\\Picardfunctor_{X/B}$", "MATH_0006": "$T \\mapsto \\Pic(X_T)$", "MATH_0007": "$B$", "MATH_0008": "$\\{U_i \\to U\\}$", "MATH_0009": "$\\xi|_{U_i}$", "MATH_0010": "$\\mathcal{L}_i$", "MATH_0011": "$X_{U_i}$", "MATH_0012": "$(U_i \\to B, \\mathcal{L}_i)$", "MATH_0013": "$\\Picardstack_{X/B}$", "MATH_0014": "$U_i$", "MATH_0015": "$\\xi|_{U_i}$", "MATH_0016": "$U$", "MATH_0017": "$B$", "MATH_0018": "$\\mathcal{L}, \\mathcal{N}$", "MATH_0019": "$X_U$", "MATH_0020": "$\\Picardfunctor_{X/B}(U)$", "MATH_0021": "$\\{U_i \\to U\\}$", "MATH_0022": "$\\mathcal{L}|_{X_{U_i}}$", "MATH_0023": "$\\mathcal{N}|_{X_{U_i}}$", "MATH_0024": "$(U \\to B, \\mathcal{L})|_{U_i} \\to (U \\to B, \\mathcal{N})|_{U_i}$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{stacks-morphisms-definition-gerbe}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{stacks-definition-gerbe-over-stack-in-groupoids}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{stacks-lemma-when-gerbe}", "REF_0004": "\\ref{quot-lemma-pic-over-pic}", "REF_0005": "\\ref{quot-situation-pic}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\medskip", "STRUCT_0002": "\\noindent", "STRUCT_0003": "\\medskip", "STRUCT_0004": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:a63906461098414e7504dc2ebd4e7a2ef90ceff31794ae9318fdb47ec9507209", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:ffaf4988484586d34dd08f327402fe0e393aeb427188c1d07c8ae374aa098eb5", "source_text": "The definition of <MATH_0001> being\na gerbe is given in Morphisms of Stacks, Definition\n<REF_0001>, which in turn refers to\nStacks, Definition <REF_0002>.\nTo prove it, we will check conditions (2)(a) and (2)(b) of\nStacks, Lemma <REF_0003>. This follows immediately from\nQuot, Lemma <REF_0004>; here is a detailed explanation.\n\n<STRUCT_0001><STRUCT_0002>\nCondition (2)(a).\nSuppose that <MATH_0002> for some scheme <MATH_0003> over <MATH_0004>.\nSince <MATH_0005> is the fppf sheafification of the rule\n<MATH_0006> on schemes over <MATH_0007>\n(Quot, Situation <REF_0005>), we see that there exists an\nfppf covering <MATH_0008> such that <MATH_0009> corresponds\nto some invertible module <MATH_0010> on <MATH_0011>.\nThen <MATH_0012> is an object of\n<MATH_0013> over <MATH_0014> mapping to <MATH_0015>.\n\n<STRUCT_0003><STRUCT_0004>\nCondition (2)(b). Suppose that <MATH_0016> is a scheme over <MATH_0017> and\n<MATH_0018> are invertible modules on <MATH_0019>\nwhich map to the same element of <MATH_0020>.\nThen there exists an fppf covering <MATH_0021>\nsuch that <MATH_0022> is isomorphic to <MATH_0023>.\nThus we find isomorphisms between\n<MATH_0024>\nas desired.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:859b65d0d61e7003184956b20854768a4de450d106a5343ad54dc0d7ffcceb22", "unit_id": "tag:0DME:proof"}
